{
  "analysis": "The review describes player-versus-player competition through repeated matches against other players and explicitly describes a pay-to-win structure in which spending provides an advantage for progressing. I considered Illusion of Control, but the review does not claim that outcomes or matchmaking are secretly manipulated; it only says skill alone is insufficient. I rejected Power Creep because buffing disliked cards does not show that a purchased item lost value, and rejected Grinding because card spamming is an opponent tactic rather than repetitive player activity required for progress.",
